4. GITHUB FORKING — AN HONEST NOTE
================================================================================

This matters, and pretending otherwise would make the rest of this document
less credible rather than more.

This repository is public on GitHub. By hosting it publicly, JohnsonXCorp has
accepted GitHub's Terms of Service, section D.5 ("License Grant to Other
Users"), which grants every GitHub user the right to VIEW and FORK this
repository within GitHub. That grant is real, it takes precedence over this
licence for that narrow purpose, and this licence does not and cannot revoke
it.

What that GitHub grant does NOT give anyone:

  - any right to use the Software outside GitHub;
  - any right to host, deploy, publish, or serve it anywhere;
  - any right to modify it beyond what GitHub's own service requires;
  - any right to distribute it off-platform;
  - any right to remove the notices, or to claim authorship;
  - any right to use it commercially.

In GitHub's own words, absent any other licence, other users may only view and
fork. Every other right named in section 3 above remains reserved. A fork that
is deployed, redistributed, rebranded, or shipped is outside the GitHub grant
and is an infringement of copyright.

If you want more than GitHub's default grant, ask. Licensing enquiries:
https://github.com/ThePastor/read-fast/issues

